=== Statement 3: n = 5 labels in F_11 (phi -> 4) ===
R_5 HNF d1,d2 = 1 11  phi^5-1 = (2, 5)  phi^3*(4-phi) = (2, 5)
cycle (C-order): ['1/13', '16/13', '8/13', '4/13', '2/13'] labels: [3, 1, 4, 5, 9] label set == H: True  == -H: False
cycle (C-order): ['-5', '-14', '-7', '-20', '-10'] labels: [8, 10, 7, 6, 2] label set == H: False  == -H: True
table order 1/13,2/13,4/13,8/13,16/13 -> [3, 9, 5, 4, 1]
table order -5,-14,-7,-20,-10 -> [8, 10, 7, 6, 2]
label(0) = 0 ; 4 has order 5
C acts as x4 on labels: True
4^4 mod 11 = 3 ; <3> = [1, 3, 4, 5, 9] ; <4> = [1, 3, 4, 5, 9] ; <5> = [1, 3, 4, 5, 9]

=== Statement 4: G_5 ===
|<x+1,4x>| = 55  |<x+1,3x>| = 55  equal: True  == {ax+b: a in H}: True
orbit of {0,1}: 55 of 55  stabilizer size: 1
orbit of arc (0,1) == Paley QR_11 arcs: True  |arcs| = 55
Borel(PSL(2,11)) on F_11 == G_5: False  |Borel| = 11

=== Statement 5: n = 10 ===
phi^10-1 = (33, 55)  = 11*phi^5 = (33, 55)  HNF d1,d2,x = 11 11 0
#points period|10 = 123  #primitive period 10 = 110
primitive points -> distinct cells: True  all beta != 0: True
points in beta=0 cells: ['-1', '-10', '-14', '-2', '-20', '-5', '-7', '0', '1/13', '16/13', '2/13', '4/13', '8/13'] count 13
C^5 acts as (a,b)->(a,-b) on the 110 primitive points (direct iteration): True
period-5 point with R_5-label l sits in R_10 cell (2l, 0): True
